    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Yordan Alvarez**, who anchors the offense with an elite 82.97 efficiency score against the vulnerable Elmer Rodr\u00edguez (5.91 xERA). We are also prioritizing stolen base potential to maintain our edge, making **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.09) a must-start; while he faces a platoon disadvantage against Eduardo Rodriguez, the combination of a favorable xERA and his high-frequency base-stealing threat against a slower delivery allows him to outperform his baseline. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (72.66) and **Junior Caminero** (73.04) are strong plays, with **Junior Caminero** benefiting from a premium #3 lineup slot and a favorable matchup against Melton, providing a rare combination of stability and ceiling that we require to climb the standings.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves the final OF/Utility spots, where **Lars Nootbaar** (53.69) narrowly missed the cut. Despite his strong projection, the optimizer preferred the superior raw power and platoon profiles of **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Christian Yelich**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Trea Turner** (54.24), who is dealing with a tough matchup against Bryan Woo; while his base score is high, the negative adjustment for Woo\u2019s skill level keeps him in a lower tier compared to the explosive potential of **Yordan Alvarez**. We remain heavily reliant on several \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions for **Gary Sanchez**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, and **Carson Benge**; should those batting orders shift significantly downward, we may be forced to pivot to our bench depth to preserve our strict game-cap management.",
